  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "During the Roswell affair of 1947, when the Army in New Mexico announced it had recovered a \"flying disc\" and then said it was a weather balloon, General Carl Spaatz, a top air commander, flew to Texas. That is where the recovered parts were supposedly taken before going on to Wright-Patterson, an Air Force base in Ohio. An online researcher who goes by the name RedPandaKoala tells Michels this, without naming a source, as a sign that the recovery mattered at the highest level."
